DarwinBoot USB receiver: "upload" (fastboot get_staged FILE) sends back the 2 MiB at 0x80D00000 (PROPOSALS.md P1, step 1)

Apply in UniXNU/drivers/DarwinBoot (git apply -p1), on top of the local UsbRamdisk.h (the USB RAM disk receiver).
ruan's stock DT reserves ramoops@80D00000 (2 MiB: two 256 KiB dmesg records, the 512 KiB console zone at 0x80D80000, 1 MiB pmsg).
The host runs `fastboot -s unixnu-ramdisk get_staged prev.bin` before `stage`; scripts/read-ramoops.py parses it. Read only.
Needs 0004-ruanpkg-ramoops-map.patch: without the memory-map entry UEFI has no mapping there and the copy faults.

--- a/DarwinBootPkg/Driver/UsbRamdisk.h
+++ b/DarwinBootPkg/Driver/UsbRamdisk.h
